<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 3 Best in Slot Gear list for Unholy Death Knight DPS in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Trial of the Grand Crusader. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">
<span class="c6">Best in Slot Gear for Unholy Death Knight DPS Phase 3</span></h2>ToC brings about a (mostly) standardized item level for raid difficulties, meaning we're no longer forced to pick between tier and higher item level gear from hardmodes.<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Strength - is still the absolute best stat for Unholy Death Knights, this will not change throughout the expansion.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Hit - to at least 8% Melee Hit  so your ghoul, gargoyle, and army of the dead as well as main hand specials will be capped, any point of hit after this will increase your spell hit and white auto attack hit chance. <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=50138/nerves-of-cold-steel">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_dualwield.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nerves of Cold Steel</span></a> does not affect your summon or spell hit, but does work for your own melee attacks and specials.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Haste - because we value increasing our gargoyles attack speed so much, on top of the base attack speed gain of haste, this stat is incredibly attractive to us.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Crit - is a great stat because of how it empowers our AoE as not only can our blood plague crit now with our new tier, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=49655/wandering-plague">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_callofbone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wandering Plague</span></a> is also based off of our crit rating.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Expertise - Expertise has less of a gain for Death Knight's compared to most classes, as our special abilities don't charge us runes if they're dodged, but that strike will still be delayed the lost GCD, and your white hits can be dodged.</div></li></ol>
<div style="text-align: -webkit-center;"></div>
<br/>
<br/>With the change in how Hardmode gear works this tier, the focus on Ilevel over stat preferences is largely done away with, instead allowing us to wear off pieces and tier that give us the best possible stats without losing out on additional strength. With that, our four set is incredibly strong this tier, for both frost and unholy, and makes us a very real option for prio'ing those pieces to. Focus on completing your four set, even using 245 tier until you get heroic tier, above all else. <br/>
